                <pb facs="0443" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg421"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Count
                            Sclopis</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 11.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Agent of the United States, has the honor to transmit herewith
                    to Count Sclopis the following copy of a telegram received from the Secretary of
                    State of the United States this day, and to ask to have it considered as a
                    further appendix to the Counter Case of United States:</p>
                <p>“Since March 22, additional claims for capture and destruction and damage by
                    interruption of voyage have been filed to the amount of five hundred and five
                    thousand eight hundred and forty-nine dollars forty-six cents, and claims for
                    increased insurance premiums to the amount of three hundred and thirty-four
                    thousand nine hundred and thirty-three dollars ninety-eight cents.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">“FISH.”</p>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor to renew to Count Sclopis the assurance of his
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. C. BANCROFT DAVIS.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
